@{
    ViewBag.Title = "Home Page";
}

<div class="section">
    <h3>System Overview</h3>
    <p>
        Welcome to the Third Normal Films Movie Rental Management System.
        This web-based application provides authorised staff with access to
        the company's movie rental database and associated rental records.
    </p>
    <p>
        The system supports viewing, searching, and managing movie information
        including titles, genres, actors, rental availability, and historical
        loan activity across store locations.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="section">
    <h3>Movie Catalogue</h3>
    <p>
        Use the navigation menu above to browse the movie collection.
        Movies can be searched and filtered by title, genre, and actor
        to quickly locate specific titles within the database.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Browse all movies in the catalogue</li>
        <li>Filter movies by title and genre</li>
        <li>Search for movies featuring specific actors</li>
        <li>View detailed movie information and rental history</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class="section">
    <h3>Movie Management</h3>
    <p>
        Authorised users can add new movies to the database using the
        Movie Creation page. The system validates entered information
        and stores new records directly within the existing rental database.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Create new movie records</li>
        <li>Maintain consistent catalogue information</li>
        <li>Automatically associate movie details and posters</li>
        <li>Access detailed information for individual titles</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class="section">
    <h3>Data Source</h3>
    <p>
        This system connects directly to the existing Third Normal Films
        PostgreSQL database. The application retrieves and displays movie,
        actor, genre, copy, store, and rental information without modifying
        the underlying database structure.
    </p>
</div>